@copilot Simplify the Couchbase Common 3.0 test wiring in `instrumentation/couchbase/couchbase-common-3.0/javaagent/build.gradle.kts` on this PR. Drop the `unitTests` dependency block: the javaagent testing convention supplies `testing-common`, which exports `:instrumentation-api-incubator` and `opentelemetry-sdk-testing`, and neither moved test nor the helpers they exercise uses `:javaagent-extension-api`. Register the two variants directly on `unitTests().executions { ... }` instead of looking up the suite by name.

Keep the default, `logs`, and `logs/dup` modes, their existing task names, the shared classpath, agent-free execution, and `check` wiring. Leave the shared variant classifier, tests, and docs unchanged. Run the three focused Couchbase Common tasks: `unitTests`, `unitTestsExceptionSignalLogs`, and `unitTestsExceptionSignalLogsDup`.

Update this existing draft PR directly on `open-telemetry/opentelemetry-java-instrumentation` branch `copilot/copilotmigrate-jodd-http-test`. Keep the cloud-assigned branch name and don't create or request a new PR or replacement branch. If GitHub creates a follow-up branch itself, keep its assigned name.

